279
00:16:06,137 --> 00:16:10,904
Yes, I bought a bunch of Japanese books.

280
00:16:10,927 --> 00:16:13,413
How many did you get?

281
00:16:13,436 --> 00:16:16,170
I bought five.

282
00:16:16,193 --> 00:16:18,770
Did you get a dictionary too?

283
00:16:18,793 --> 00:16:22,830
Yes, I picked up a dictionary as well.

284
00:16:22,853 --> 00:16:27,420
You have so many books at your place, don’t you?

285
00:16:27,443 --> 00:16:32,111
Yes, I’ve got loads of books at home.

286
00:16:32,134 --> 00:16:35,172
Including a lot of English books.

287
00:16:35,196 --> 00:16:39,045
Do you have a lot of friends too?

288
00:16:39,069 --> 00:16:42,802
Yes, I’ve got plenty of friends in America.

289
00:16:42,825 --> 00:16:46,475
And lots of friends in Japan too.

290
00:16:46,498 --> 00:16:49,970
How many hours do you study every day?

291
00:16:49,993 --> 00:16:53,760
I study for three hours every day.

292
00:16:53,783 --> 00:16:58,416
Three hours? That’s a lot!

293
00:16:58,439 --> 00:17:02,973
Yeah, I study a lot every day.

294
00:17:02,996 --> 00:17:06,482
Did you study a lot yesterday too?

295
00:17:06,505 --> 00:17:10,958
No, I only studied for an hour yesterday.

296
00:17:10,982 --> 00:17:15,193
Well, it *was* Sunday.

297
00:17:15,216 --> 00:17:19,432
Yeah, I took it easy on Sunday.

298
00:17:19,455 --> 00:17:20,955
Scene 9: Japanese Food and Learning

299
00:17:20,955 --> 00:17:24,989
Is Japanese food delicious?

300
00:17:25,012 --> 00:17:28,945
Yes, it’s absolutely delicious.

301
00:17:28,968 --> 00:17:32,057
Is sushi good?

302
00:17:32,081 --> 00:17:36,847
Yes, sushi is amazing.

303
00:17:36,870 --> 00:17:39,604
How about ramen?

304
00:17:39,627 --> 00:17:43,093
Ramen is great too.

305
00:17:43,116 --> 00:17:46,483
Though it can be a little spicy.

306
00:17:46,506 --> 00:17:50,539
Is learning Japanese interesting?

307
00:17:50,562 --> 00:17:56,229
Yes, it’s really fascinating.

308
00:17:56,253 --> 00:18:00,419
Are kanji difficult?

309
00:18:00,442 --> 00:18:05,076
Yes, kanji are really tough.

310
00:18:05,099 --> 00:18:07,596
What about katakana?

311
00:18:07,619 --> 00:18:11,019
Katakana isn’t difficult.

312
00:18:11,042 --> 00:18:12,877
It’s actually pretty easy.

313
00:18:12,900 --> 00:18:16,467
Is Tokyo a beautiful city?

314
00:18:16,490 --> 00:18:21,657
Yes, Tokyo is a very beautiful city.

315
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:24,213
How about Kyoto?

316
00:18:24,236 --> 00:18:27,570
Kyoto is a beautiful city.

317
00:18:27,594 --> 00:18:30,672
It has many ancient temples.

318
00:18:30,695 --> 00:18:35,345
Is your school big, Mr. Smith?

319
00:18:35,369 --> 00:18:40,835
Yes, my school is very big.

320
00:18:40,858 --> 00:18:43,732
Are the classrooms new?

321
00:18:43,756 --> 00:18:49,044
Yes, the classrooms are very new.

322
00:18:49,067 --> 00:18:51,924
Are the teachers strict?

323
00:18:51,948 --> 00:18:57,314
No, my teachers aren’t strict at all.

324
00:18:57,337 --> 00:18:59,504
They’re very kind.

325
00:18:59,527 --> 00:19:03,207
Is your house new, Mr. Smith?

326
00:19:03,230 --> 00:19:08,464
No, my house isn’t new.

327
00:19:08,487 --> 00:19:10,253
It’s old.

328
00:19:10,276 --> 00:19:12,843
Are the rooms spacious?

329
00:19:12,866 --> 00:19:17,364
No, the rooms aren’t spacious.

330
00:19:17,387 --> 00:19:19,073
They’re small.

331
00:19:19,097 --> 00:19:22,097
Are you busy every day?

332
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:27,001
Yes, I’m very busy every day.

333
00:19:27,024 --> 00:19:29,678
Is it hot today?

334
00:19:29,702 --> 00:19:34,069
No, it’s not hot today.

335
00:19:34,092 --> 00:19:36,337
It’s a little cold.

336
00:19:36,361 --> 00:19:37,861
Scene 10: Mr. Smith's Preferences

337
00:19:37,861 --> 00:19:41,794
Do you like meat, Mr. Smith?

338
00:19:41,817 --> 00:19:46,250
Yes, I love meat.

339
00:19:46,273 --> 00:19:48,707
How about fish?

340
00:19:48,730 --> 00:19:52,819
I don’t really like fish.

341
00:19:52,842 --> 00:19:55,609
Do you like vegetables?

342
00:19:55,632 --> 00:19:59,798
No, I don’t like vegetables.

343
00:19:59,821 --> 00:20:03,794
What’s your favorite food?

344
00:20:03,818 --> 00:20:07,252
I love tempura the most.

345
00:20:07,275 --> 00:20:10,372
What do you like to drink?

346
00:20:10,395 --> 00:20:12,961
I like coffee.

347
00:20:12,985 --> 00:20:15,418
I don’t like tea.

348
00:20:15,441 --> 00:20:18,328
What’s your favorite sport?

349
00:20:18,352 --> 00:20:21,188
I like soccer.

350
00:20:21,212 --> 00:20:23,812
I don’t like tennis.

351
00:20:23,835 --> 00:20:27,768
Are you good at singing, Mr. Smith?

352
00:20:27,791 --> 00:20:32,791
No, I’m not good at singing.

353
00:20:32,814 --> 00:20:34,432
I’m bad at it.

354
00:20:34,455 --> 00:20:38,289
Is John good at singing?

355
00:20:38,312 --> 00:20:43,446
Yes, John is very good at singing.

356
00:20:43,470 --> 00:20:47,480
Are you good at cooking, Mr. Smith?

357
00:20:47,503 --> 00:20:52,080
Yes, I’m good at cooking.

358
00:20:52,104 --> 00:20:54,918
I cook every day.

359
00:20:54,941 --> 00:20:57,316
That’s wonderful!

360
00:20:57,340 --> 00:21:00,306
Are you good at Japanese?

361
00:21:00,329 --> 00:21:05,147
No, I’m still not very good at Japanese.

362
00:21:05,171 --> 00:21:06,744
I’m bad at it.

363
00:21:06,767 --> 00:21:09,167
How about English?

364
00:21:09,190 --> 00:21:13,823
English is my native language, so I’m good at it.

365
00:21:13,846 --> 00:21:18,013
Let’s have tempura for lunch today.

366
00:21:18,036 --> 00:21:19,907
That sounds great!

367
00:21:19,931 --> 00:21:22,264
Let’s eat tempura.

368
00:21:22,287 --> 00:21:25,020
Let’s go to that restaurant.

369
00:21:25,043 --> 00:21:29,777
Yes, let's go to that lovely café!

370
00:21:29,799 --> 00:21:32,933
And let's grab some coffee there.

371
00:21:32,956 --> 00:21:36,125
Sure, let's have some together!

372
00:21:36,149 --> 00:21:37,649
Scene 11: Directions Made Easy / Basic Japanese for Asking Directions

373
00:21:37,649 --> 00:21:39,649
Excuse me.

374
00:21:39,672 --> 00:21:43,284
Excuse me, could you give me directions?

375
00:21:43,307 --> 00:21:46,274
Of course, I'd be happy to help!

376
00:21:46,297 --> 00:21:48,663
Where are you headed?

377
00:21:48,686 --> 00:21:50,941
I'm trying to get to the train station.

378
00:21:50,965 --> 00:21:54,299
But I'm not sure how to get there.

379
00:21:54,323 --> 00:21:56,589
The train station, you say?

380
00:21:56,612 --> 00:22:00,746
It's a bit of a walk from here.

381
00:22:00,769 --> 00:22:03,035
I see.

382
00:22:03,059 --> 00:22:06,825
I'm really in a bind here.

383
00:22:06,848 --> 00:22:11,068
Here, take a look at this old map.

384
00:22:11,091 --> 00:22:13,825
Okay, let me see.

385
00:22:13,848 --> 00:22:18,022
We're right here.

386
00:22:18,046 --> 00:22:20,123
Got it.

387
00:22:20,147 --> 00:22:22,313
Got it.

388
00:22:22,336 --> 00:22:26,870
First, go straight down this road.

389
00:22:26,893 --> 00:22:29,459
Straight ahead, got it.

390
00:22:29,482 --> 00:22:35,020
Then, take a right at that big intersection.

391
00:22:35,044 --> 00:22:37,423
Right turn, okay.

392
00:22:37,447 --> 00:22:42,256
There's an old bank there.

393
00:22:42,280 --> 00:22:45,613
Is it that white building?

394
00:22:45,636 --> 00:22:49,769
No, it's the blue one.

395
00:22:49,792 --> 00:22:51,769
Got it.

396
00:22:51,792 --> 00:22:56,359
Next to the bank, you'll find a new department store.

397
00:22:56,382 --> 00:22:58,551
The department store?

398
00:22:58,575 --> 00:23:03,708
Yes, and in front of it, there's a bus stop.

399
00:23:03,731 --> 00:23:05,946
The bus stop, right.

400
00:23:05,970 --> 00:23:11,171
Take the number one bus from there.

401
00:23:11,194 --> 00:23:13,995
Bus number one, got it.

402
00:23:14,018 --> 00:23:19,194
That bus goes straight to the station—super convenient!

403
00:23:19,217 --> 00:23:21,684
How long is the bus ride?

404
00:23:21,707 --> 00:23:24,722
About five minutes.

405
00:23:24,745 --> 00:23:28,145
It's close, so you'll be there in no time!

406
00:23:28,168 --> 00:23:30,001
That's a relief!

407
00:23:30,024 --> 00:23:31,827
I feel so much better now.

408
00:23:31,850 --> 00:23:37,417
It's really hot today, so make sure to drink plenty of water.

409
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:39,929
Will do!

410
00:23:39,953 --> 00:23:43,519
Take care on your way!

411
00:23:43,542 --> 00:23:46,996
Thank you so much for your help!

412
00:23:47,019 --> 00:23:48,519
Scene 12: Polite Requests / Asking for Permission in Conversation

413
00:23:48,519 --> 00:23:50,519
Excuse me.

414
00:23:50,542 --> 00:23:54,216
Is it okay if I take a photo here?

415
00:23:54,240 --> 00:23:59,131
No, I'm afraid you can't take photos here.

416
00:23:59,154 --> 00:24:02,001
Oh, I see.

417
00:24:02,024 --> 00:24:04,191
Why not?

418
00:24:04,214 --> 00:24:10,014
There are a lot of old photographs here.

419
00:24:10,037 --> 00:24:11,672
Got it.

420
00:24:11,696 --> 00:24:15,729
Then, is it okay if I go in there?

421
00:24:15,752 --> 00:24:20,559
No, I'm afraid you can't go in there either.

422
00:24:20,582 --> 00:24:23,116
That's off-limits too?

423
00:24:23,139 --> 00:24:29,139
Yes, that's the company president's office.

424
00:24:29,162 --> 00:24:30,775
Got it.

425
00:24:30,798 --> 00:24:35,031
So, where *can* I take a break?

426
00:24:35,054 --> 00:24:38,343
The break room is over there.

427
00:24:38,366 --> 00:24:41,933
You can smoke there if you'd like.

428
00:24:41,956 --> 00:24:44,589
Can I have some tea?

429
00:24:44,612 --> 00:24:46,281
Yes, I do.

430
00:24:46,305 --> 00:24:49,601
Tea or juice, either is fine.

431
00:24:49,625 --> 00:24:51,960
We have plenty.

432
00:24:51,983 --> 00:24:54,117
Great!

433
00:24:54,140 --> 00:24:57,475
Can I use this computer?

434
00:24:57,498 --> 00:25:02,965
No, you can't use that computer.

435
00:25:02,988 --> 00:25:05,562
Whose computer is it?

436
00:25:05,585 --> 00:25:08,852
It's Mr. Tanaka's computer.

437
00:25:08,875 --> 00:25:11,441
Don't touch it.

438
00:25:11,464 --> 00:25:13,300
Got it.

439
00:25:13,324 --> 00:25:17,691
Then, can I check my phone?

440
00:25:17,714 --> 00:25:19,450
Yes, I do.

441
00:25:19,473 --> 00:25:22,307
Your phone is fine.

442
00:25:22,330 --> 00:25:24,426
That's a relief!

443
00:25:24,449 --> 00:25:29,699
But don't play around during work hours.

444
00:25:29,723 --> 00:25:32,332
Yes, I understand.

445
00:25:32,356 --> 00:25:34,189
I'll be careful.

446
00:25:34,212 --> 00:25:39,079
Alright, please come to that room at 12 o'clock.

447
00:25:39,102 --> 00:25:41,768
Yes, I understand.

448
00:25:41,791 --> 00:25:44,358
I appreciate it.

449
00:25:44,381 --> 00:25:45,881
Scene 13: A Phone Conversation

450
00:25:45,881 --> 00:25:50,097
Hello, what are you doing right now?

451
00:25:50,120 --> 00:25:55,559
Hey, I'm just listening to music at home.

452
00:25:55,582 --> 00:25:57,228
Nice.

453
00:25:57,251 --> 00:26:00,385
What kind of music are you listening to?

454
00:26:00,408 --> 00:26:04,492
I'm listening to some old Japanese songs.

455
00:26:04,515 --> 00:26:06,281
Oh, I see.

456
00:26:06,304 --> 00:26:09,271
Have you eaten yet?

457
00:26:09,294 --> 00:26:11,061
Yeah.

458
00:26:11,084 --> 00:26:14,284
I just had a bento a little while ago.

459
00:26:14,307 --> 00:26:17,164
Did you go anywhere today?

460
00:26:17,187 --> 00:26:19,254
Hmm.

461
00:26:19,277 --> 00:26:24,526
It's been raining all day, so I've just been at home.

462
00:26:24,550 --> 00:26:26,124
Oh, I see.

463
00:26:26,147 --> 00:26:29,514
What's Mark doing right now?

464
00:26:29,537 --> 00:26:34,580
Mark is sleeping in the next room.

465
00:26:34,603 --> 00:26:37,471
What? He's already asleep?

466
00:26:37,494 --> 00:26:39,694
That's early.

467
00:26:39,717 --> 00:26:41,650
Yeah.

468
00:26:41,673 --> 00:26:47,807
He worked a lot from this morning, so he's really tired.

469
00:26:47,830 --> 00:26:49,763
I see.

470
00:26:49,786 --> 00:26:52,953
What time are you waking up tomorrow?

471
00:26:52,976 --> 00:26:56,619
I'll wake up at 6 tomorrow.

472
00:26:56,642 --> 00:26:59,128
That's early in the morning.

473
00:26:59,151 --> 00:27:01,318
Are you working tomorrow too?

474
00:27:01,341 --> 00:27:03,189
Yeah.

475
00:27:03,212 --> 00:27:06,745
Yeah, I have work from the morning.

476
00:27:06,768 --> 00:27:09,035
That sounds tough.

477
00:27:09,058 --> 00:27:12,591
Is it still raining outside?

478
00:27:12,614 --> 00:27:14,448
Yeah.

479
00:27:14,471 --> 00:27:17,743
Yeah, it's still pouring.

480
00:27:17,767 --> 00:27:20,007
And the wind is strong too.

481
00:27:20,030 --> 00:27:23,438
So, you can't go out, huh?

482
00:27:23,461 --> 00:27:25,529
Oh, I see.

483
00:27:25,553 --> 00:27:29,489
That's why I'm reading a book at home.

484
00:27:29,512 --> 00:27:32,712
What book are you reading?

485
00:27:32,735 --> 00:27:36,668
I'm reading a Japanese textbook.

486
00:27:36,691 --> 00:27:38,225
That's impressive!

487
00:27:38,248 --> 00:27:41,281
Keep up the good work with your studies!

488
00:27:41,304 --> 00:27:42,798
Thank you.

489
00:27:42,822 --> 00:27:45,355
I'll be in touch again soon.

490
00:27:45,378 --> 00:27:46,878
Scene 14: Introducing My Family

491
00:27:46,878 --> 00:27:50,568
Whose photo is this?

492
00:27:50,591 --> 00:27:55,225
This is a photo of my family.

493
00:27:55,248 --> 00:27:58,663
Wow, what a lovely photo!

494
00:27:58,686 --> 00:28:01,886
How many people are in your family?

495
00:28:01,909 --> 00:28:05,320
There are four of us in my family.

496
00:28:05,344 --> 00:28:09,184
I have a wife and two children.

497
00:28:09,207 --> 00:28:13,090
Who is this tall person?

498
00:28:13,114 --> 00:28:16,880
This is my son.

499
00:28:16,903 --> 00:28:20,270
Your son has big eyes, doesn't he?

500
00:28:20,293 --> 00:28:25,582
Yes, my son has long hair.

501
00:28:25,606 --> 00:28:29,139
And he's a great singer too!

502
00:28:29,162 --> 00:28:31,261
Nice.

503
00:28:31,285 --> 00:28:35,485
Who is this adorable girl?

504
00:28:35,508 --> 00:28:39,041
This is my daughter.

505
00:28:39,064 --> 00:28:42,731
My daughter is six years old this year.

506
00:28:42,754 --> 00:28:46,587
Your daughter has such tiny hands!

507
00:28:46,610 --> 00:28:52,856
Yes, she does. She goes to school every day now.

508
00:28:52,879 --> 00:28:55,246
Every day?

509
00:28:55,269 --> 00:28:58,436
That sounds lively!

510
00:28:58,459 --> 00:29:02,592
Yes, it's very lively every day.

511
00:29:02,615 --> 00:29:05,548
Where is your wife?

512
00:29:05,571 --> 00:29:09,771
This is my wife, the person on the right.

513
00:29:09,794 --> 00:29:13,128
Is your wife a quiet person?

514
00:29:13,152 --> 00:29:17,620
No, my wife is quite the talker.

515
00:29:17,643 --> 00:29:20,416
She's very energetic!

516
00:29:20,440 --> 00:29:24,687
That sounds like a fun family.

517
00:29:24,711 --> 00:29:30,111
Yeah. Everyone in my family loves cameras.

518
00:29:30,134 --> 00:29:34,753
So, you must have lots of great photos.

519
00:29:34,777 --> 00:29:38,629
Yes. We take photos every day.

520
00:29:38,652 --> 00:29:41,300
That’s so nice.

521
00:29:41,324 --> 00:29:45,793
My family is in Vietnam right now.

522
00:29:45,816 --> 00:29:49,817
That must be tough.

523
00:29:49,841 --> 00:29:55,379
Yeah. But we talk on the phone every day.

524
00:29:55,402 --> 00:29:56,902
Scene 15: Sunday Photography Outing

525
00:29:56,902 --> 00:30:01,195
What are your plans for this Sunday?

526
00:30:01,219 --> 00:30:07,785
This Sunday, I’m going to the park to take photos.

527
00:30:07,808 --> 00:30:09,688
The park?

528
00:30:09,712 --> 00:30:11,545
That sounds great!

529
00:30:11,568 --> 00:30:14,207
Which park?

530
00:30:14,230 --> 00:30:19,564
The big park in the center of town.

531
00:30:19,587 --> 00:30:24,323
It’s quiet and beautiful there—perfect for photos.

532
00:30:24,346 --> 00:30:31,512
Yeah. The weather this Sunday is supposed to be nice and cool.

533
00:30:31,535 --> 00:30:34,735
Who are you going with?

534
00:30:34,758 --> 00:30:38,958
I’m going with my friend Mark.

535
00:30:38,981 --> 00:30:42,348
Does Mark have a camera too?

536
00:30:42,371 --> 00:30:43,841
Yes, I do.

537
00:30:43,865 --> 00:30:49,398
Mark just bought a new, big camera.

538
00:30:49,421 --> 00:30:51,621
I see.

539
00:30:51,644 --> 00:30:55,577
I’d love to go to that park too!

540
00:30:55,600 --> 00:30:59,055
Let's go together then.

541
00:30:59,079 --> 00:31:01,116
Does that work for you?

542
00:31:01,140 --> 00:31:03,173
I'm so happy!

543
00:31:03,196 --> 00:31:08,196
Let's meet in front of the station at 9 AM on Sunday.

544
00:31:08,219 --> 00:31:10,287
Got it.

545
00:31:10,311 --> 00:31:13,154
How are you getting to the station?

546
00:31:13,178 --> 00:31:16,311
I'll bike there.

547
00:31:16,334 --> 00:31:19,067
It's close to the station, after all.

548
00:31:19,090 --> 00:31:21,890
I'll take the bus.

549
00:31:21,913 --> 00:31:26,280
Buses are convenient and affordable—great choice!

550
00:31:26,303 --> 00:31:27,936
Yeah.

551
00:31:27,959 --> 00:31:32,560
Is there a good restaurant near the park?

552
00:31:32,584 --> 00:31:34,455
Yes, I do.

553
00:31:34,478 --> 00:31:39,812
There's a new and delicious restaurant right in front of the park.

554
00:31:39,835 --> 00:31:43,235
New *and* old?

555
00:31:43,258 --> 00:31:45,858
That’s interesting!

556
00:31:45,880 --> 00:31:50,337
Their curry is cheap *and* tasty, you know.

557
00:31:50,361 --> 00:31:55,100
Then let’s have lunch there!

558
00:31:55,123 --> 00:31:57,923
Yeah, let’s do that.

559
00:31:57,946 --> 00:32:00,439
I’m really looking forward to it!

560
00:32:00,462 --> 00:32:01,962
Scene 16: Movie Impressions

561
00:32:01,962 --> 00:32:06,035
I saw a new movie yesterday.

562
00:32:06,059 --> 00:32:07,711
I see.

563
00:32:07,734 --> 00:32:10,703
What movie did you watch?

564
00:32:10,727 --> 00:32:14,460
That famous animated film.

565
00:32:14,483 --> 00:32:17,516
Oh, *that* movie!

566
00:32:17,539 --> 00:32:19,673
How was it?

567
00:32:19,696 --> 00:32:25,096
I thought it was a bit too long.

568
00:32:25,119 --> 00:32:28,552
How long was it?

569
00:32:28,575 --> 00:32:31,387
Around three hours.

570
00:32:31,410 --> 00:32:33,943
I was so exhausted afterward.

571
00:32:33,966 --> 00:32:37,500
Three hours *is* long.

572
00:32:37,523 --> 00:32:39,894
Was it interesting?

573
00:32:39,917 --> 00:32:45,410
Hmm, I didn’t think it was that fun.

574
00:32:45,434 --> 00:32:48,116
Oh, really?

575
00:32:48,139 --> 00:32:51,306
Why wasn’t it fun?

576
00:32:51,329 --> 00:32:55,147
The story was a little hard to follow.

577
00:32:55,170 --> 00:32:57,805
I didn’t really get it.

578
00:32:57,829 --> 00:32:59,862
I see.

579
00:32:59,885 --> 00:33:03,485
Was it too complex for kids?

580
00:33:03,508 --> 00:33:04,975
Yes, I do.

581
00:33:04,998 --> 00:33:08,731
I think it would be *very* hard for kids to understand.

582
00:33:08,754 --> 00:33:11,572
How was the music?

583
00:33:11,595 --> 00:33:15,962
The music was really beautiful—I loved it.

584
00:33:15,985 --> 00:33:19,672
Nice when the music is good, isn’t it?

585
00:33:19,696 --> 00:33:24,496
Yeah, but the theater seats were so hard!

586
00:33:24,519 --> 00:33:27,285
That sounds rough.

587
00:33:27,308 --> 00:33:30,316
Did your butt start hurting?

588
00:33:30,339 --> 00:33:31,906
Yes, I do.

589
00:33:31,929 --> 00:33:35,227
My butt hurt *so* much!

590
00:33:35,251 --> 00:33:40,231
That’s why three hours felt even longer.

591
00:33:40,254 --> 00:33:42,331
Exactly!

592
00:33:42,355 --> 00:33:45,208
I even got sleepy halfway through.

593
00:33:45,231 --> 00:33:48,664
Movie theaters *are* dark, after all.

594
00:33:48,687 --> 00:33:51,721
I get sleepy there all the time too.

595
00:33:51,744 --> 00:33:55,977
But I tried my best until the end.

596
00:33:56,000 --> 00:33:57,835
That's impressive!

597
00:33:57,858 --> 00:34:01,392
Did your friend say anything?

598
00:34:01,415 --> 00:34:06,248
My friend said it was really funny.

599
00:34:06,271 --> 00:34:09,889
Everyone has different opinions, huh?

600
00:34:09,913 --> 00:34:15,648
Yeah, my friend even said they'd watch it again next week.

601
00:34:15,671 --> 00:34:17,766
Really?

602
00:34:17,790 --> 00:34:20,556
They must have loved it.

603
00:34:20,579 --> 00:34:22,227
Yes, I do.

604
00:34:22,250 --> 00:34:25,653
I don’t think I want to watch it again, though.

605
00:34:25,677 --> 00:34:29,810
Next time, let’s watch something shorter.

606
00:34:29,833 --> 00:34:31,466
That sounds good.

607
00:34:31,489 --> 00:34:36,130
I’d love to watch a fun comedy next.

608
00:34:36,154 --> 00:34:38,233
That’s a great idea!

609
00:34:38,256 --> 00:34:41,789
I’d like to join you next time.

610
00:34:41,812 --> 00:34:43,312
Scene 17: Meeting Preparation and Schedules

611
00:34:43,312 --> 00:34:47,769
Did you see Mark today?

612
00:34:47,792 --> 00:34:51,827
No, I haven’t seen him yet today.

613
00:34:51,851 --> 00:34:54,339
Did something happen?

614
00:34:54,362 --> 00:35:01,530
Mark said he can’t come here tomorrow.

615
00:35:01,553 --> 00:35:05,287
Wait, he can’t come tomorrow?

616
00:35:05,310 --> 00:35:07,243
Why not?

617
00:35:07,266 --> 00:35:14,204
He said he has an important errand from the morning.

618
00:35:14,227 --> 00:35:16,161
I see.

619
00:35:16,184 --> 00:35:19,584
What should we do about tomorrow’s meeting?

620
00:35:19,607 --> 00:35:25,740
He said he’d finish preparing the documents today.

621
00:35:25,763 --> 00:35:28,412
That’s a relief.

622
00:35:28,435 --> 00:35:32,269
Where is Mark now?

623
00:35:32,292 --> 00:35:37,058
He’s working in another room right now.

624
00:35:37,081 --> 00:35:38,781
Got it.

625
00:35:38,804 --> 00:35:41,061
I’ll go check on him later.

626
00:35:41,084 --> 00:35:46,918
Oh, and Mark left a message for you.

627
00:35:46,941 --> 00:35:49,074
What’s the message?

628
00:35:49,097 --> 00:35:54,264
He said he returned the book to Mr. Tanaka.

629
00:35:54,287 --> 00:35:56,087
A book?

630
00:35:56,110 --> 00:35:58,477
What kind of book?

631
00:35:58,500 --> 00:36:02,466
He said it was a Japanese dictionary.

632
00:36:02,489 --> 00:36:04,124
Got it.

633
00:36:04,147 --> 00:36:06,590
I’ll let Mr. Tanaka know.

634
00:36:06,614 --> 00:36:08,694
I appreciate it.

635
00:36:08,718 --> 00:36:12,685
Mark seemed in a hurry.

636
00:36:12,708 --> 00:36:15,741
He must be busy preparing for his errand.

637
00:36:15,764 --> 00:36:22,036
No, he said he’s been busy all week.

638
00:36:22,059 --> 00:36:25,116
I hope he’s okay.

639
00:36:25,140 --> 00:36:26,550
I’m worried about him.

640
00:36:26,574 --> 00:36:32,857
He said he’s been sleeping well every night, so he’s fine.

641
00:36:32,880 --> 00:36:35,485
That’s reassuring to hear.

642
00:36:35,509 --> 00:36:41,043
He said he’d come in early next Monday.

643
00:36:41,066 --> 00:36:42,866
Got it.

644
00:36:42,889 --> 00:36:45,364
I’ll talk to him on Monday.

645
00:36:45,387 --> 00:36:46,847
Yes, I do.

646
00:36:46,871 --> 00:36:49,204
That’s all for the message.

647
00:36:49,227 --> 00:36:51,828
Thanks for letting me know.

648
00:36:51,852 --> 00:36:56,866
No problem. I’ll let you know if anything else comes up.

649
00:36:56,889 --> 00:36:58,123
Yes, I do.

650
00:36:58,146 --> 00:37:00,346
I appreciate it.

651
00:37:00,369 --> 00:37:01,869
Scene 18: Hobbies and Cooking

652
00:37:01,869 --> 00:37:05,202
What’s your hobby?

653
00:37:05,225 --> 00:37:09,431
My hobby is cooking.

654
00:37:09,454 --> 00:37:12,254
Cooking? That sounds wonderful.

655
00:37:12,277 --> 00:37:14,765
Do you cook every day?

656
00:37:14,789 --> 00:37:16,189
Yes, I do.

657
00:37:16,212 --> 00:37:20,480
I really love cooking.

658
00:37:20,503 --> 00:37:23,508
What kind of dishes do you usually make?

659
00:37:23,531 --> 00:37:26,777
I often cook Japanese food.

660
00:37:26,800 --> 00:37:29,488
I make a mean nikujaga (Japanese meat and potato stew).

661
00:37:29,512 --> 00:37:32,245
Wow, nikujaga?

662
00:37:32,268 --> 00:37:34,285
I'd love to try it!

663
00:37:34,309 --> 00:37:38,475
How about having a party at my place sometime?

664
00:37:38,498 --> 00:37:40,349
That sounds great!

665
00:37:40,373 --> 00:37:42,464
I'd love to come!

666
00:37:42,488 --> 00:37:45,126
What’s your hobby?

667
00:37:45,149 --> 00:37:49,116
I love singing songs.

668
00:37:49,139 --> 00:37:52,106
Singing? That’s great!

669
00:37:52,129 --> 00:37:54,462
Where do you usually sing?

670
00:37:54,485 --> 00:37:57,652
I often go to karaoke and sing.

671
00:37:57,674 --> 00:38:00,679
Mark mentioned something about you.

672
00:38:00,703 --> 00:38:03,937
What did Mark say?

673
00:38:03,960 --> 00:38:07,960
He said you’re an amazing singer.

674
00:38:07,982 --> 00:38:11,749
Wait, Mark said that?

675
00:38:11,773 --> 00:38:13,707
Oh, that’s embarrassing.

676
00:38:13,730 --> 00:38:17,096
You should sing at the party!

677
00:38:17,119 --> 00:38:18,815
Got it.

678
00:38:18,839 --> 00:38:20,973
I’ll sing a little.

679
00:38:20,996 --> 00:38:23,238
I’m really looking forward to it!

680
00:38:23,262 --> 00:38:26,495
I’ll prepare lots of food.

681
00:38:26,518 --> 00:38:30,764
I love buying sweets, so I’ll bring some.

682
00:38:30,788 --> 00:38:32,388
Thank you!

683
00:38:32,411 --> 00:38:35,218
I love sweets.

684
00:38:35,242 --> 00:38:37,724
Let’s invite Mark too.

685
00:38:37,747 --> 00:38:42,747
Yeah. Mark’s great at playing the guitar.

686
00:38:42,770 --> 00:38:44,637
Really?

687
00:38:44,660 --> 00:38:47,831
We can all enjoy music together!

688
00:38:47,855 --> 00:38:52,221
Yes, it’ll be a lively party!

689
00:38:52,244 --> 00:38:55,178
I can’t wait for Sunday!

690
00:38:55,201 --> 00:38:58,860
Yes, I’ll see you on Sunday!

691
00:38:58,883 --> 00:39:00,383
Scene 19: Convenience Break on a Hot Day

692
00:39:00,383 --> 00:39:04,552
Whew, we’ve been walking for a while.

693
00:39:04,575 --> 00:39:07,184
I’m exhausted.

694
00:39:07,208 --> 00:39:09,341
That sounds good.

695
00:39:09,364 --> 00:39:13,498
It’s so hot outside right now.

696
00:39:13,521 --> 00:39:16,754
I’m really thirsty.

697
00:39:16,777 --> 00:39:18,311
Yeah.

698
00:39:18,334 --> 00:39:21,701
There’s a convenience store over there.

699
00:39:21,724 --> 00:39:25,217
Want to grab something at the convenience store?

700
00:39:25,241 --> 00:39:29,274
I’d like to buy some cold tea.

701
00:39:29,297 --> 00:39:31,130
That sounds great!

702
00:39:31,153 --> 00:39:34,753
I’m craving some sparkling water.

703
00:39:34,776 --> 00:39:38,710
Are you getting anything to eat?

704
00:39:38,733 --> 00:39:44,466
I’m full right now, so I don’t need anything.

705
00:39:44,489 --> 00:39:46,061
I see.

706
00:39:46,084 --> 00:39:50,151
I’m a little hungry, though.

707
00:39:50,174 --> 00:39:54,189
Well then, why not grab an onigiri or something?

708
00:39:54,213 --> 00:39:56,946
Will do!

709
00:39:56,969 --> 00:40:00,010
I love salmon onigiri.

710
00:40:00,033 --> 00:40:03,800
Convenience store ice cream is delicious too, you know.

711
00:40:03,823 --> 00:40:06,637
Ice cream?

712
00:40:06,660 --> 00:40:08,794
That sounds great!

713
00:40:08,817 --> 00:40:13,883
But maybe I shouldn’t eat anything right now?

714
00:40:13,906 --> 00:40:15,963
Why not?

715
00:40:15,987 --> 00:40:20,405
It's almost dinnertime in an hour.

716
00:40:20,429 --> 00:40:23,965
Oh, I forgot about that.

717
00:40:23,988 --> 00:40:27,885
Then I'll skip the rice balls.

718
00:40:27,908 --> 00:40:31,642
Yeah, let's just get drinks.

719
00:40:31,665 --> 00:40:33,431
Got it.

720
00:40:33,454 --> 00:40:36,462
Let's buy something cold to drink.

721
00:40:36,486 --> 00:40:39,720
I'll pay for it.

722
00:40:39,743 --> 00:40:42,543
Really? Are you sure?

723
00:40:42,566 --> 00:40:43,932
Excuse me.

724
00:40:43,955 --> 00:40:49,591
You always help me out, so this is the least I can do.

725
00:40:49,614 --> 00:40:51,548
Thank you!

726
00:40:51,571 --> 00:40:54,704
Then I'll have some tea, please.

727
00:40:54,727 --> 00:40:58,961
Alright, let's go into the store.

728
00:40:58,985 --> 00:41:02,830
It's so nice and cool inside the store.

729
00:41:02,853 --> 00:41:05,292
It really is.

730
00:41:05,315 --> 00:41:07,849
I don't even want to leave.

731
00:41:07,873 --> 00:41:11,040
Where are the baskets?

732
00:41:11,063 --> 00:41:14,396
They're near the entrance.

733
00:41:14,419 --> 00:41:16,186
Got it.

734
00:41:16,209 --> 00:41:18,142
I'll go get one.

735
00:41:18,165 --> 00:41:19,665
Scene 20: Memories of Our Trip

736
00:41:19,665 --> 00:41:23,520
How was your trip last week?

737
00:41:23,543 --> 00:41:28,758
It was so much fun!

738
00:41:28,782 --> 00:41:31,315
Where did you go?

739
00:41:31,338 --> 00:41:34,378
I went to Hokkaido.

740
00:41:34,401 --> 00:41:36,635
It was my first time.

741
00:41:36,658 --> 00:41:40,265
Oh, Hokkaido, huh?

742
00:41:40,288 --> 00:41:42,466
Wasn't it cold?

743
00:41:42,490 --> 00:41:47,144
It wasn't too bad, thankfully.

744
00:41:47,167 --> 00:41:49,900
The weather was great every day.

745
00:41:49,923 --> 00:41:52,656
That's great to hear!

746
00:41:52,679 --> 00:41:55,134
What did you eat?

747
00:41:55,157 --> 00:41:59,003
I had a lot of sushi.

748
00:41:59,027 --> 00:42:01,227
It was so delicious.

749
00:42:01,250 --> 00:42:06,283
I'm jealous! I want to eat sushi too.

750
00:42:06,306 --> 00:42:11,573
The fish was so fresh, it didn't smell at all.

751
00:42:11,597 --> 00:42:14,130
Did you try ramen?

752
00:42:14,153 --> 00:42:15,920
Yeah.

753
00:42:15,943 --> 00:42:19,425
I had miso ramen at night.

754
00:42:19,448 --> 00:42:21,300
It really warmed me up.

755
00:42:21,323 --> 00:42:24,732
Was the trip expensive?

756
00:42:24,755 --> 00:42:29,957
The flight was a bit pricey, but the hotel was cheap.

757
00:42:29,981 --> 00:42:33,215
Was the hotel nice?

758
00:42:33,239 --> 00:42:34,617
Yeah.

759
00:42:34,640 --> 00:42:39,007
It was new and really beautiful.

760
00:42:39,030 --> 00:42:42,196
Did you visit any tourist spots?

761
00:42:42,219 --> 00:42:45,953
I went to see a big lake.

762
00:42:45,975 --> 00:42:48,811
It was so peaceful and beautiful.

763
00:42:48,835 --> 00:42:51,568
Did you take a lot of photos?

764
00:42:51,591 --> 00:42:55,724
I took about 100 pictures on my phone.

765
00:42:55,747 --> 00:42:57,714
I'll show you later.

766
00:42:57,737 --> 00:42:59,304
Thank you.

767
00:42:59,327 --> 00:43:02,369
Did you buy any souvenirs?

768
00:43:02,393 --> 00:43:06,126
I got some delicious cookies.

769
00:43:06,149 --> 00:43:08,765
Here, this is for you.

770
00:43:08,789 --> 00:43:11,643
Wow, thank you!

771
00:43:11,666 --> 00:43:14,033
I'm so happy!

772
00:43:14,056 --> 00:43:20,235
The trip was fun, but I'm exhausted from the long travel time.

773
00:43:20,258 --> 00:43:23,534
How many hours was the flight?

774
00:43:23,557 --> 00:43:27,575
It took about two hours from Tokyo.

775
00:43:27,599 --> 00:43:31,011
Two hours is a bit long, isn't it?

776
00:43:31,034 --> 00:43:34,434
But it turned into such great memories.

777
00:43:34,457 --> 00:43:36,352
Yeah.

778
00:43:36,376 --> 00:43:40,778
It was so good, I want to go again!

779
00:43:40,801 --> 00:43:44,286
Next time, I want to go with you!

780
00:43:44,310 --> 00:43:45,946
Nice.

781
00:43:45,970 --> 00:43:49,770
You mentioned that Hokkaido is beautiful in winter, right?

782
00:43:49,793 --> 00:43:53,526
Then let's go in winter next time!

783
00:43:53,549 --> 00:43:55,049
Scene 21: Meet the New Teacher

784
00:43:55,049 --> 00:44:00,703
Who’s that person reading a book over there?

785
00:44:00,726 --> 00:44:05,304
Oh, you mean the one near the window?

786
00:44:05,328 --> 00:44:10,895
Yes, the one wearing the black hat.

787
00:44:10,918 --> 00:44:16,285
That’s the new teacher who started last week.

788
00:44:16,308 --> 00:44:18,341
I see.

789
00:44:18,364 --> 00:44:21,810
What’s their name?

790
00:44:21,834 --> 00:44:25,067
It’s Mr./Ms. Tanaka.

791
00:44:25,090 --> 00:44:30,773
Mr./Ms. Tanaka? What do they teach?

792
00:44:30,797 --> 00:44:35,205
They teach Japanese history.

793
00:44:35,228 --> 00:44:38,897
Oh, a history teacher?

794
00:44:38,920 --> 00:44:41,054
They look young.

795
00:44:41,077 --> 00:44:48,810
Yeah, everyone who talked to them yesterday said they’re really kind.

796
00:44:48,833 --> 00:44:51,306
That’s great to hear.

797
00:44:51,329 --> 00:44:54,342
I want to talk to them too.

798
00:44:54,366 --> 00:44:59,808
I wonder what book they’re reading.

799
00:44:59,832 --> 00:45:03,065
That’s a really big book.

800
00:45:03,088 --> 00:45:05,421
Is it a dictionary?

801
00:45:05,444 --> 00:45:11,616
No, it’s a book with lots of old photos.

802
00:45:11,640 --> 00:45:15,976
Oh, they’re moving to the next room.

803
00:45:16,000 --> 00:45:20,267
Looks like they’re going to talk to the other teacher over there.

804
00:45:20,290 --> 00:45:24,103
Their bag is really nice too.

805
00:45:24,126 --> 00:45:29,726
Yeah, they said they bought it in Kyoto.

806
00:45:29,749 --> 00:45:33,525
Kyoto? That sounds amazing.

807
00:45:33,548 --> 00:45:36,236
I want to go there too.

808
00:45:36,260 --> 00:45:41,627
I heard they studied at a university in Kyoto.

809
00:45:41,650 --> 00:45:44,816
That’s why they love Kyoto so much.

810
00:45:44,839 --> 00:45:46,909
Makes sense.

811
00:45:46,933 --> 00:45:51,466
Oh, they just looked over here and smiled!

812
00:45:51,489 --> 00:45:54,023
Wait, really?

813
00:45:54,046 --> 00:45:56,779
That’s a little embarrassing.

814
00:45:56,802 --> 00:45:59,335
It’s fine, don’t worry.

815
00:45:59,358 --> 00:46:01,558
Let’s go say hi!

816
00:46:01,581 --> 00:46:06,048
Not now—they’re talking to someone else.

817
00:46:06,071 --> 00:46:07,804
That sounds good.

818
00:46:07,827 --> 00:46:11,639
Let’s wait here until they’re done.

819
00:46:11,663 --> 00:46:16,863
Okay. Oh, who’s that person eating cake over there?

820
00:46:16,886 --> 00:46:20,552
That’s Mark.

821
00:46:20,575 --> 00:46:23,109
He’s always eating, isn’t he?

822
00:46:23,132 --> 00:46:28,465
Hehe, Mark *really* loves food.

823
00:46:28,488 --> 00:46:33,288
Yeah, and the food he cooks is delicious too.

824
00:46:33,311 --> 00:46:37,956
I want to try his cooking sometime.

825
00:46:37,979 --> 00:46:42,312
Then let’s have a party together next time!

826
00:46:42,335 --> 00:46:43,835
Scene 22: Last-Minute Chaos Before the Report Deadline

827
00:46:43,835 --> 00:46:48,724
Mark, have you submitted that report yet?

828
00:46:48,748 --> 00:46:53,435
No, I haven’t even started writing it.

829
00:46:53,458 --> 00:46:55,991
Wait, seriously?

830
00:46:56,014 --> 00:46:58,912
It’s due tomorrow morning, right?

831
00:46:58,936 --> 00:47:03,936
Yeah, I know, but I’m not done yet.

832
00:47:03,959 --> 00:47:05,935
Why not?

833
00:47:05,958 --> 00:47:09,002
You’ve had plenty of time, though?

834
00:47:09,026 --> 00:47:13,761
My computer crashed, and I lost all the data.

835
00:47:13,784 --> 00:47:16,793
That sounds rough.

836
00:47:16,816 --> 00:47:19,149
Is it working now?

837
00:47:19,172 --> 00:47:25,187
Yeah, I borrowed a friend’s laptop and I’m working on it now.

838
00:47:25,211 --> 00:47:27,611
How much have you written so far?

839
00:47:27,634 --> 00:47:29,867
About half, maybe?

840
00:47:29,890 --> 00:47:34,457
No, I’ve barely written anything.

841
00:47:34,480 --> 00:47:36,680
I’m freaking out.

842
00:47:36,703 --> 00:47:41,103
You’ll have to pull an all-nighter at this rate.

843
00:47:41,126 --> 00:47:44,926
Yeah, I’m planning to stay up and finish it.

844
00:47:44,949 --> 00:47:47,515
Are you sure you’re okay physically?

845
00:47:47,538 --> 00:47:50,338
Don’t push yourself too hard, okay?

846
00:47:50,361 --> 00:47:52,561
Thank you!

847
00:47:52,584 --> 00:47:56,624
But if I don’t turn it in, I’ll be in big trouble.

848
00:47:56,648 --> 00:48:00,421
Have you asked anyone to check the kanji for you yet?

849
00:48:00,445 --> 00:48:04,845
No, I haven’t asked anyone.

850
00:48:04,868 --> 00:48:08,736
Want me to help you with that?

851
00:48:08,759 --> 00:48:11,359
Wait, really?

852
00:48:11,382 --> 00:48:13,749
That would be a huge help!

853
00:48:13,772 --> 00:48:17,744
Show me what you’ve got as you finish it.

854
00:48:17,768 --> 00:48:19,737
Got it.

855
00:48:19,760 --> 00:48:23,832
But I haven’t even finished the first page yet.

856
00:48:23,855 --> 00:48:26,388
Hurry up!

857
00:48:26,411 --> 00:48:29,296
Time’s ticking!

858
00:48:29,320 --> 00:48:33,939
Got it—I’ll start typing as fast as I can.

859
00:48:33,963 --> 00:48:37,234
Have you eaten dinner yet?

860
00:48:37,257 --> 00:48:41,424
No, I haven’t eaten anything.

861
00:48:41,446 --> 00:48:43,784
I’m starving.

862
00:48:43,807 --> 00:48:48,974
I’ll grab something from the convenience store for you.

863
00:48:48,997 --> 00:48:50,397
Excuse me.

864
00:48:50,421 --> 00:48:53,388
Two rice balls, please.

865
00:48:53,411 --> 00:48:55,491
Got it.

866
00:48:55,514 --> 00:48:57,985
I’ll get some tea too.

867
00:48:58,009 --> 00:48:59,648
Thank you!

868
00:48:59,671 --> 00:49:02,684
I’ll pay you back later.

869
00:49:02,708 --> 00:49:04,641
Don’t worry about it.

870
00:49:04,664 --> 00:49:07,513
Just focus on finishing that report.

871
00:49:07,536 --> 00:49:09,349
Yes, I do.

872
00:49:09,373 --> 00:49:14,551
I’m so lucky to have such a kind senior.

873
00:49:14,574 --> 00:49:16,449
Yeah, yeah.

874
00:49:16,473 --> 00:49:19,906
Cut the flattery and get to work!

875
00:49:19,929 --> 00:49:21,938
Got it.

876
00:49:21,962 --> 00:49:24,695
I’ll concentrate and do my best.

877
00:49:24,718 --> 00:49:26,218
Scene 23: Picking from the Menu – A Conversation

878
00:49:26,218 --> 00:49:29,418
There are so many options on the menu!

879
00:49:29,441 --> 00:49:31,508
What are you thinking of getting?

880
00:49:31,530 --> 00:49:33,697
It really is.

881
00:49:33,720 --> 00:49:39,153
I can’t decide between meat or fish.

882
00:49:39,177 --> 00:49:44,510
Do you usually prefer meat or fish?

883
00:49:44,533 --> 00:49:48,791
I like meat more than fish.

884
00:49:48,815 --> 00:49:52,582
How about this beef bowl, then?

885
00:49:52,605 --> 00:49:54,872
That looks delicious!

886
00:49:54,895 --> 00:49:57,262
That sounds great!

887
00:49:57,285 --> 00:50:00,618
What about this fish set meal?

888
00:50:00,641 --> 00:50:06,374
Fish is popular because it's good for your health.

889
00:50:06,397 --> 00:50:08,997
Which one would you like?

890
00:50:09,020 --> 00:50:10,894
Have you decided yet?

891
00:50:10,918 --> 00:50:15,051
I'll go with this chicken curry.

892
00:50:15,074 --> 00:50:18,074
I love spicy food.

893
00:50:18,097 --> 00:50:20,503
Curry sounds great.

894
00:50:20,527 --> 00:50:23,410
I can smell it from here.

895
00:50:23,434 --> 00:50:27,567
Which do you prefer, udon or soba?

896
00:50:27,590 --> 00:50:31,323
I like soba better.

897
00:50:31,346 --> 00:50:34,080
I love cold soba noodles.

898
00:50:34,103 --> 00:50:38,070
This place is famous for its soba, too.

899
00:50:38,093 --> 00:50:40,528
People say it's delicious.

900
00:50:40,552 --> 00:50:43,490
Oh, really?

901
00:50:43,513 --> 00:50:46,925
Now I can't decide!

902
00:50:46,948 --> 00:50:49,882
Take your time.

903
00:50:49,905 --> 00:50:52,381
We've got plenty of time.

904
00:50:52,405 --> 00:50:58,005
Which juice do you recommend, apple or orange?

905
00:50:58,028 --> 00:51:02,761
I prefer apple juice—it's sweeter.

906
00:51:02,784 --> 00:51:06,751
Then I'll have the orange juice.

907
00:51:06,774 --> 00:51:09,340
I love sour flavors.

908
00:51:09,363 --> 00:51:14,232
Our tastes are so different!

909
00:51:14,255 --> 00:51:16,111
That's interesting.

910
00:51:16,135 --> 00:51:21,511
Yeah, that's why eating together is so fun.

911
00:51:21,535 --> 00:51:23,168
That sounds good.

912
00:51:23,191 --> 00:51:27,391
Oh, sorry—could we order, please?

913
00:51:27,414 --> 00:51:31,547
Wait, I haven't decided yet!

914
00:51:31,570 --> 00:51:34,337
Oh, my bad!

915
00:51:34,360 --> 00:51:38,160
The server's coming—you'd better decide fast!

916
00:51:38,183 --> 00:51:42,659
Then I'll go with the beef bowl.

917
00:51:42,682 --> 00:51:45,572
I'm starving!

918
00:51:45,596 --> 00:51:48,267
So you went with meat, huh?

919
00:51:48,290 --> 00:51:49,979
That's a relief!

920
00:51:50,003 --> 00:51:54,970
Yep, I really want to eat lots of meat.

921
00:51:54,993 --> 00:52:00,033
The set meal comes with miso soup—that's a plus!

922
00:52:00,056 --> 00:52:05,941
Yeah, warm soup is so comforting.

923
00:52:05,964 --> 00:52:09,964
Let's talk about tomorrow's plans while we wait for our food.

924
00:52:09,987 --> 00:52:14,405
Sure, what time are we leaving tomorrow?

925
00:52:14,429 --> 00:52:15,929
Scene 24: Memories of the Year

926
00:52:15,929 --> 00:52:20,362
This class is almost over.

927
00:52:20,386 --> 00:52:22,152
I'm going to miss it.

928
00:52:22,175 --> 00:52:24,192
It really is.

929
00:52:24,216 --> 00:52:29,016
This year flew by so fast.

930
00:52:29,039 --> 00:52:34,872
Which season was your favorite this year?

931
00:52:34,895 --> 00:52:41,128
I loved autumn the most—it was so beautiful.

932
00:52:41,151 --> 00:52:43,085
Autumn?

933
00:52:43,108 --> 00:52:46,766
Why do you like autumn the best?

934
00:52:46,789 --> 00:52:51,646
We went to the mountains and saw the fall foliage together.

935
00:52:51,670 --> 00:52:55,121
Oh, that trip!

936
00:52:55,144 --> 00:52:58,115
We took so many photos.

937
00:52:58,139 --> 00:53:04,577
Yeah, the weather was perfect—it wasn't cold at all.

938
00:53:04,600 --> 00:53:09,233
What event was your most memorable this year?

939
00:53:09,257 --> 00:53:14,624
The winter speech contest was so nerve-wracking.

940
00:53:14,647 --> 00:53:20,454
Yeah, you practiced so hard every day!

941
00:53:20,477 --> 00:53:27,717
Yes, I read the longest passage in class.

942
00:53:27,740 --> 00:53:32,274
I didn’t win any awards, but I did really well.

943
00:53:32,297 --> 00:53:33,988
Thank you!

944
00:53:34,012 --> 00:53:36,845
It’s become a wonderful memory.

945
00:53:36,868 --> 00:53:42,201
Which subject did you find the most challenging to study?

946
00:53:42,224 --> 00:53:47,358
I think honorifics were the hardest.

947
00:53:47,381 --> 00:53:53,320
Even Japanese people make mistakes with honorifics—they’re tough!

948
00:53:53,343 --> 00:54:00,029
But Mr. Tanaka’s teaching style was the easiest to understand.

949
00:54:00,053 --> 00:54:01,453
That sounds good.

950
00:54:01,476 --> 00:54:06,010
Mr. Tanaka was always so kind.

951
00:54:06,033 --> 00:54:11,366
Who did you talk to the most among your classmates?

952
00:54:11,389 --> 00:54:16,189
I talked the most with Mark.

953
00:54:16,212 --> 00:54:21,378
Mark is always so lively and funny, isn’t he?

954
00:54:21,401 --> 00:54:27,070
Yeah, the class always felt brighter when he was around.

955
00:54:27,094 --> 00:54:32,431
Where are we having next week’s class party?

956
00:54:32,455 --> 00:54:37,929
The restaurant near school is the cheapest and most spacious.

957
00:54:37,953 --> 00:54:43,153
Then let’s make our final memories there together.

958
00:54:43,176 --> 00:54:44,754
Yes, I do.

959
00:54:44,777 --> 00:54:48,144
I’ll make sure not to forget my camera.

960
00:54:48,167 --> 00:54:52,767
I’m planning to bring lots of homemade snacks.

961
00:54:52,790 --> 00:54:55,604
Wow, I can’t wait!

962
00:54:55,627 --> 00:54:59,278
Your cooking is always the best.

963
00:54:59,302 --> 00:55:02,435
I’ll do my best to make them delicious.

964
00:55:02,458 --> 00:55:04,269
Looking forward to it!

965
00:55:04,293 --> 00:55:05,793
Scene 25: Future Path and Dreams – A Career in Trade

966
00:55:05,793 --> 00:55:10,759
Have you decided on your plans after graduation?

967
00:55:10,782 --> 00:55:12,221
Yes, I do.

968
00:55:12,245 --> 00:55:17,214
I plan to keep working in Japan.

969
00:55:17,237 --> 00:55:19,680
At a Japanese company?

970
00:55:19,704 --> 00:55:22,116
That’s wonderful!

971
00:55:22,139 --> 00:55:25,073
What kind of work will you do?

972
00:55:25,096 --> 00:55:31,392
I want to use what I’ve studied to work in trade.

973
00:55:31,415 --> 00:55:34,458
A career in trade?

974
00:55:34,481 --> 00:55:37,648
Will you use a lot of English?

975
00:55:37,671 --> 00:55:39,271
Yes, I do.

976
00:55:39,294 --> 00:55:43,627
It’s a job where I’ll use both English and Japanese.

977
00:55:43,650 --> 00:55:49,450
That’s why you were studying so hard at school until late every day.

978
00:55:49,473 --> 00:55:51,331
Yeah.

979
00:55:51,354 --> 00:55:56,554
I want to get even better at Japanese and really excel in my work.

980
00:55:56,577 --> 00:55:59,581
What’s your dream for the future?

981
00:55:59,605 --> 00:56:02,412
What kind of person do you want to become?

982
00:56:02,435 --> 00:56:09,635
I want to stay in this country long-term and gain lots of experience.

983
00:56:09,658 --> 00:56:14,791
You’ll definitely become a great professional.

984
00:56:14,814 --> 00:56:16,654
Thank you!

985
00:56:16,678 --> 00:56:21,334
It’s my first job, so I’m really excited.

986
00:56:21,357 --> 00:56:25,723
Do you plan to keep living in this town?

987
00:56:25,746 --> 00:56:30,992
No, I’m moving to Osaka next year.

988
00:56:31,016 --> 00:56:33,782
The cost of living is cheaper there.

989
00:56:33,805 --> 00:56:39,138
You mentioned that Osaka has really delicious food.

990
00:56:39,161 --> 00:56:43,642
Yeah, I’m planning to eat lots of takoyaki!

991
00:56:43,666 --> 00:56:45,800
That sounds great!

992
00:56:45,823 --> 00:56:50,105
When you get a raise, make sure to invite me.

993
00:56:50,128 --> 00:56:53,261
Hehe, of course!

994
00:56:53,284 --> 00:56:55,884
I’ll treat you to a feast!

995
00:56:55,907 --> 00:56:58,198
Promise?

996
00:56:58,221 --> 00:57:02,155
I want to eat some high-quality meat.

997
00:57:02,178 --> 00:57:06,911
I’ll work hard, earn lots of money, and become rich!

998
00:57:06,934 --> 00:57:13,218
Before starting your new job, is there anything special you’re preparing?

999
00:57:13,242 --> 00:57:18,135
This winter, I plan to buy myself a kimono.

1000
00:57:18,159 --> 00:57:21,027
A kimono?

1001
00:57:21,050 --> 00:57:23,858
Can you put it on by yourself?

1002
00:57:23,882 --> 00:57:27,500
No, not yet.

1003
00:57:27,524 --> 00:57:32,057
That's why I'm planning to learn by watching YouTube.

1004
00:57:32,080 --> 00:57:37,255
It'd be so cool if you could dress yourself in a kimono.

1005
00:57:37,278 --> 00:57:43,478
Yeah, I want to wear it for Japanese New Year and visit a shrine.

1006
00:57:43,502 --> 00:57:47,158
Your dreams just keep growing, don't they?

1007
00:57:47,182 --> 00:57:49,115
I'm rooting for you!

1008
00:57:49,138 --> 00:57:50,671
Thank you!

1009
00:57:50,694 --> 00:57:55,177
Tell me about your plans next time too.

1010
00:57:55,201 --> 00:57:56,701
Scene 26: Holiday Travel Plans

1011
00:57:56,701 --> 00:57:59,634
The long weekend is coming up soon.

1012
00:57:59,657 --> 00:58:03,490
Have you decided on your weekend trip plans yet?

1013
00:58:03,513 --> 00:58:05,047
Yes, I do.

1014
00:58:05,070 --> 00:58:08,346
I'm going somewhere with friends.

1015
00:58:08,369 --> 00:58:10,536
That sounds great!

1016
00:58:10,559 --> 00:58:13,726
Somewhere far?

1017
00:58:13,749 --> 00:58:17,549
No, not too far.

1018
00:58:17,572 --> 00:58:19,461
I see.

1019
00:58:19,484 --> 00:58:22,084
How are you getting there?

1020
00:58:22,107 --> 00:58:24,540
By Shinkansen?

1021
00:58:24,563 --> 00:58:28,251
No, not the Shinkansen.

1022
00:58:28,275 --> 00:58:30,909
We're planning to go by car.

1023
00:58:30,932 --> 00:58:33,298
By car?

1024
00:58:33,321 --> 00:58:36,291
Who's driving?

1025
00:58:36,315 --> 00:58:38,884
A friend is driving.

1026
00:58:38,908 --> 00:58:42,558
I can't drive.

1027
00:58:42,581 --> 00:58:44,514
I see.

1028
00:58:44,537 --> 00:58:47,829
Is it a famous tourist spot?

1029
00:58:47,853 --> 00:58:49,469
Yes, I do.

1030
00:58:49,492 --> 00:58:53,226
We're going to a town with a famous hot spring.

1031
00:58:53,249 --> 00:58:55,620
A hot spring?

1032
00:58:55,643 --> 00:58:58,110
That sounds amazing!

1033
00:58:58,133 --> 00:59:00,025
Yeah.

1034
00:59:00,048 --> 00:59:04,581
I'll soak in the hot spring and relax.

1035
00:59:04,604 --> 00:59:07,606
Have you booked your accommodation yet?

1036
00:59:07,630 --> 00:59:09,363
Yes, I do.

1037
00:59:09,386 --> 00:59:13,725
I booked an old inn in the mountains.

1038
00:59:13,749 --> 00:59:16,353
In the mountains?

1039
00:59:16,377 --> 00:59:19,421
The scenery must be beautiful.

1040
00:59:19,445 --> 00:59:21,096
Yes, I do.

1041
00:59:21,120 --> 00:59:26,453
But since it's a long weekend, I think the roads will be crowded.

1042
00:59:26,476 --> 00:59:28,515
That sounds good.

1043
00:59:28,538 --> 00:59:32,176
You should leave early in the morning.

1044
00:59:32,200 --> 00:59:33,800
Yeah.

1045
00:59:33,823 --> 00:59:37,356
I plan to leave at five in the morning.

1046
00:59:37,379 --> 00:59:39,512
Five o'clock?

1047
00:59:39,535 --> 00:59:41,935
That's early!

1048
00:59:41,958 --> 00:59:43,525
Yes, I do.

1049
00:59:43,548 --> 00:59:46,922
Are you stopping anywhere along the way?

1050
00:59:46,946 --> 00:59:51,601
I plan to stop at a service area with delicious food.

1051
00:59:51,624 --> 00:59:53,224
That sounds great!

1052
00:59:53,247 --> 00:59:56,658
Please drive safely!

1053
00:59:56,681 --> 00:59:57,938
Yes, I do.

1054
00:59:57,961 --> 01:00:00,179
Thank you!

1055
01:00:00,203 --> 01:00:01,703
Scene 27: Desired Travel Destinations in Japan

1056
01:00:01,703 --> 01:00:06,870
Mark, where in Japan would you like to go?

1057
01:00:06,893 --> 01:00:11,508
I want to go to Mount Fuji.

1058
01:00:11,532 --> 01:00:13,609
Mount Fuji?

1059
01:00:13,632 --> 01:00:16,066
Do you want to climb it?

1060
01:00:16,089 --> 01:00:17,822
Or just see it?

1061
01:00:17,845 --> 01:00:21,331
I definitely want to climb to the top!

1062
01:00:21,355 --> 01:00:26,488
The view from the top of Mount Fuji is truly stunning.

1063
01:00:26,511 --> 01:00:28,589
I see.

1064
01:00:28,613 --> 01:00:31,752
Now I want to go even more!

1065
01:00:31,776 --> 01:00:34,709
Any other places you'd like to visit?

1066
01:00:34,732 --> 01:00:37,206
I'd love to visit Kyoto too.

1067
01:00:37,230 --> 01:00:39,196
Kyoto, huh?

1068
01:00:39,219 --> 01:00:42,862
What do you want to do in Kyoto?

1069
01:00:42,886 --> 01:00:47,452
I want to see lots of old temples and shrines.

1070
01:00:47,475 --> 01:00:49,075
That sounds great!

1071
01:00:49,098 --> 01:00:53,114
Walking around in a kimono is fun too, you know.

1072
01:00:53,138 --> 01:00:56,405
Wow, I'd love to try that!

1073
01:00:56,428 --> 01:00:59,515
I also want to try some delicious Japanese sweets.

1074
01:00:59,539 --> 01:01:04,154
Yeah, and I want to eat lots of sushi too!

1075
01:01:04,178 --> 01:01:06,311
Sushi?

1076
01:01:06,334 --> 01:01:08,267
That sounds great!

1077
01:01:08,290 --> 01:01:12,747
The fish in Japan is so fresh, after all.

1078
01:01:12,771 --> 01:01:16,137
The fish in Hokkaido is delicious too.

1079
01:01:16,160 --> 01:01:18,527
Hokkaido?

1080
01:01:18,550 --> 01:01:21,685
I'd love to go there too.

1081
01:01:21,708 --> 01:01:24,908
There are so many places you want to visit, huh?

1082
01:01:24,931 --> 01:01:29,698
Yeah, I wish I had more money and time.

1083
01:01:29,721 --> 01:01:32,054
Hehe, true.

1084
01:01:32,077 --> 01:01:35,851
Let’s start with Mount Fuji.

1085
01:01:35,875 --> 01:01:40,491
Yeah, I definitely want to go this summer!

1086
01:01:40,515 --> 01:01:43,848
Planning it is so exciting.

1087
01:01:43,871 --> 01:01:48,438
Yeah, I'm already so excited!

1088
01:01:48,461 --> 01:01:49,961
Scene 28: How to Spend Your Days Off

1089
01:01:49,961 --> 01:01:56,394
Mark, how do you usually spend your days off?

1090
01:01:56,417 --> 01:02:01,984
I watch movies at home or go shopping with friends.

1091
01:02:02,007 --> 01:02:03,859
That sounds great!

1092
01:02:03,882 --> 01:02:07,415
What kind of movies do you usually watch?

1093
01:02:07,438 --> 01:02:11,416
I often watch action movies and anime.

1094
01:02:11,440 --> 01:02:13,007
I see.

1095
01:02:13,030 --> 01:02:16,406
Where do you go shopping?

1096
01:02:16,429 --> 01:02:20,429
I go to department stores in Shibuya or Shinjuku.

1097
01:02:20,452 --> 01:02:23,230
Those are lively areas, aren’t they?

1098
01:02:23,253 --> 01:02:25,787
What do you buy?

1099
01:02:25,810 --> 01:02:29,346
I usually buy clothes and shoes.

1100
01:02:29,369 --> 01:02:31,169
That’s stylish!

1101
01:02:31,192 --> 01:02:34,959
What do you do on Sundays?

1102
01:02:34,982 --> 01:02:41,467
On Sundays, I take walks in the park or read books at a café.

1103
01:02:41,490 --> 01:02:44,338
That sounds like a peaceful day off.

1104
01:02:44,362 --> 01:02:46,035
Yes, I do.

1105
01:02:46,059 --> 01:02:50,859
I also cook or clean my room.

1106
01:02:50,882 --> 01:02:53,049
That's impressive!

1107
01:02:53,071 --> 01:02:58,950
On my days off, I do laundry or just sleep.

1108
01:02:58,974 --> 01:03:02,623
Getting lots of sleep is good for you.

1109
01:03:02,647 --> 01:03:04,180
Yeah.

1110
01:03:04,203 --> 01:03:08,570
But sometimes I feel like going out somewhere.

1111
01:03:08,593 --> 01:03:14,263
Well then, how about going to an art museum together next time you're off?

1112
01:03:14,287 --> 01:03:16,454
An art museum?

1113
01:03:16,477 --> 01:03:18,477
That sounds great!

1114
01:03:18,500 --> 01:03:22,533
We can look at paintings and have some tea.

1115
01:03:22,556 --> 01:03:23,923
Yes, I do.

1116
01:03:23,946 --> 01:03:26,612
I’d love to go with you!

1117
01:03:26,635 --> 01:03:28,648
I’m really looking forward to it!

1118
01:03:28,672 --> 01:03:31,438
Let’s go on Saturday.

1119
01:03:31,461 --> 01:03:33,261
Got it.

1120
01:03:33,284 --> 01:03:36,651
Let’s meet Saturday morning.

1121
01:03:36,674 --> 01:03:38,174
Scene 29: First Meeting and Experiences in Japan

1122
01:03:38,174 --> 01:03:43,907
Nice to meet you. Are you the new student who joined this class this month?

1123
01:03:43,930 --> 01:03:46,897
Yes, nice to meet you.

1124
01:03:46,920 --> 01:03:48,597
I’m Smith.

1125
01:03:48,620 --> 01:03:53,426
Mr. Smith, is this your first time living in Japan?

1126
01:03:53,449 --> 01:03:57,288
No, it’s not my first time.

1127
01:03:57,312 --> 01:03:59,712
Is that so?

1128
01:03:59,735 --> 01:04:03,624
Have you been to Japan before?

1129
01:04:03,647 --> 01:04:08,485
Yes, I came here once two years ago.

1130
01:04:08,508 --> 01:04:11,541
Was that for sightseeing?

1131
01:04:11,564 --> 01:04:17,564
Yes, I traveled to Kyoto and Osaka.

1132
01:04:17,587 --> 01:04:19,061
I see.

1133
01:04:19,085 --> 01:04:23,219
Have you tried any Japanese food?

1134
01:04:23,242 --> 01:04:28,484
Yes, I’ve had sushi and tempura.

1135
01:04:28,507 --> 01:04:31,107
How about natto?

1136
01:04:31,131 --> 01:04:35,009
I haven’t tried natto yet.

1137
01:04:35,032 --> 01:04:39,437
It has a bit of a smell, but it’s delicious!

1138
01:04:39,460 --> 01:04:41,279
I see.

1139
01:04:41,303 --> 01:04:43,936
I’ll give it a try next time.

1140
01:04:43,959 --> 01:04:47,326
Have you ever climbed Mount Fuji?

1141
01:04:47,349 --> 01:04:54,282
No, I’ve only seen it from a distance, but I’ve never climbed it.

1142
01:04:54,305 --> 01:04:57,913
You should definitely climb it this summer!

1143
01:04:57,937 --> 01:05:01,190
Yes, I’d love to.

1144
01:05:01,213 --> 01:05:06,179
Mr. Smith, where did you learn Japanese?

1145
01:05:06,202 --> 01:05:10,336
I studied a little at a university in the U.S.

1146
01:05:10,359 --> 01:05:14,796
Have you ever spoken with Japanese friends?

1147
01:05:14,819 --> 01:05:17,861
No, not yet.

1148
01:05:17,885 --> 01:05:22,738
There are plenty of Japanese students here, so why not give it a try?

1149
01:05:22,762 --> 01:05:26,295
Yes, I’d love to talk to them a lot.

1150
01:05:26,318 --> 01:05:27,818
Scene 30: Excuses for Being Late

1151
01:05:27,818 --> 01:05:31,951
Mark, why were you late?

1152
01:05:31,974 --> 01:05:36,552
I’ve been waiting here for a whole hour!

1153
01:05:36,576 --> 01:05:39,048
I’m really sorry about that.

1154
01:05:39,071 --> 01:05:42,238
I overslept.

1155
01:05:42,261 --> 01:05:43,716
What?

1156
01:05:43,740 --> 01:05:45,615
You overslept?

1157
01:05:45,638 --> 01:05:49,518
Were you up late last night?

1158
01:05:49,542 --> 01:05:51,219
Yes, I do.

1159
01:05:51,243 --> 01:05:55,009
I drank too much last night.

1160
01:05:55,032 --> 01:05:58,566
I have a terrible headache.

1161
01:05:58,589 --> 01:06:02,355
Drinking too much isn’t good for you.

1162
01:06:02,378 --> 01:06:07,145
Today’s meeting is important—you can’t be late.

1163
01:06:07,168 --> 01:06:10,014
Yes, I know.

1164
01:06:10,037 --> 01:06:15,004
I rushed here, so I’m really out of breath.

1165
01:06:15,027 --> 01:06:17,469
You ran here, didn’t you?

1166
01:06:17,493 --> 01:06:22,926
But from now on, you really need to go to bed earlier.

1167
01:06:22,949 --> 01:06:26,882
Yes, I’ll be more careful.

1168
01:06:26,905 --> 01:06:30,872
You’re sweating a lot.

1169
01:06:30,895 --> 01:06:34,187
You should drink some water.

1170
01:06:34,211 --> 01:06:35,811
Thank you!

1171
01:06:35,834 --> 01:06:40,167
There’s a convenience store over there—I’ll go buy some.

1172
01:06:40,190 --> 01:06:44,724
The meeting’s about to start, so hurry up.

1173
01:06:44,747 --> 01:06:48,113
Okay, I’ll be right back.

1174
01:06:48,136 --> 01:06:51,670
Are you really feeling okay?

1175
01:06:51,693 --> 01:06:55,859
I’m a little sleepy, but I’m fine.

1176
01:06:55,882 --> 01:07:00,849
You should go home early and rest after work.

1177
01:07:00,872 --> 01:07:06,605
Yes, I definitely plan to go to bed early tonight.

1178
01:07:06,628 --> 01:07:09,286
Let’s go then.

1179
01:07:09,309 --> 01:07:13,729
I’m really sorry about this.